      <div class="venue-tag">IMF-World Bank Annual Meetings Research Symposium</div>
      <h1>Global Economy in the Shadow of War</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">IMF World Economic Outlook Trends 2024-2026 &mdash; A synthesis of eight WEO editions tracking global growth, inflation, and evolving policy priorities amid rising geopolitical uncertainty.</p>
      <div class="edition-count">
        <span class="num" data-count="8" data-suffix="">8</span>
        WEO Editions Reviewed
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ===== KEY METRICS ===== -->
    <section class="metrics-strip animate delay-1" aria-label="Key Metrics">
      <div class="metric-item">
        <div class="metric-value accent" data-count="3.0" data-suffix="%" data-prefix="">3.0%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Growth 2025</div>
        <div class="metric-source">WEO Jul 2025</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-item">
        <div class="metric-value accent" data-count="3.3" data-suffix="%" data-prefix="">3.3%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Growth 2026</div>
        <div class="metric-source">WEO Jan 2026</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-item">
        <div class="metric-value accent" data-count="3.2" data-suffix="%" data-prefix="">3.2%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Growth 2027</div>
        <div class="metric-source">WEO Jan 2026</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-item">
        <div class="metric-value text">3.0&ndash;3.3%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Narrow Growth Band</div>
        <div class="metric-source">Across all editions</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-item">
        <div class="metric-value warning">Downside</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Risk Balance</div>
        <div class="metric-source">Consistent across all 8 WEOs</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== MAIN BODY ===== -->
    <div class="poster-body">

      <!-- GROWTH TRAJECTORY - FULL WIDTH CENTERPIECE -->
      <section class="section section-full animate delay-2" aria-label="Global Growth Projections">
        <div class="section-label">Section 01</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Global Growth Projections: A Narrow Band of Mediocrity</h2>
        <div class="chart-wrapper">
          <div class="chart-container">
            <div class="pre-pandemic-label">Pre-pandemic avg: ~3.8%</div>
            <canvas id="growthChart" role="img" aria-label="Line chart showing IMF global growth projections from July 2024 to April 2026, with forecasts for 2025 and 2026 hovering in the 3.0-3.3% range, well below the pre-pandemic average of 3.8%"></canvas>
          </div>
          <p class="chart-note">Source: IMF World Economic Outlook, Jul 2024 &ndash; Apr 2026. Dashed line indicates pre-pandemic historical average (~3.8%). &ldquo;Slowing&rdquo; and &ldquo;Renewed pressure&rdquo; entries reflect qualitative assessments where precise figures were not published.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- RISKS - LEFT COLUMN -->
      <section class="section section-left animate delay-3" aria-label="Dominant Downside Risks">
        <div class="section-label">Section 02</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Dominant Downside Risks</h2>
        <div class="risk-callout">
          <div class="risk-callout-title">
            <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
            Risk Balance: Tilted to the Downside
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom:16px;">This conclusion is consistent across all eight WEO editions reviewed&mdash;a rare unanimity in economic forecasting.</p>
          <div class="risk-grid">
            <div class="risk-item">
              <div class="risk-item-title">Trade Policy Escalation</div>
              <div class="risk-item-desc">Tariff increases and retaliatory measures from 2025 onward, with front-loading of activity temporarily masking damage.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-item">
              <div class="risk-item-title">Geopolitical Tensions</div>
              <div class="risk-item-desc">Conflicts in the Middle East, broader security concerns, and the war referenced in the April 2026 edition.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-item">
              <div class="risk-item-title">Technology Re-evaluation</div>
              <div class="risk-item-desc">Elevated expectations around AI and tech investment could face a correction, disrupting capital flows.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-item">
              <div class="risk-item-title">Persistent Services Inflation</div>
              <div class="risk-item-desc">Particularly in the United States, where inflation is projected to return to target more gradually than peers.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- INFLATION - RIGHT COLUMN -->
      <section class="section section-right animate delay-3" aria-label="Inflation and Monetary Policy">
        <div class="section-label">Section 03</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Inflation Outlook &amp; Monetary Policy</h2>
        <p class="section-body" style="margin-bottom:18px;">Global inflation has been on a declining trajectory, enabling central banks to begin easing&mdash;what the October 2024 WEO termed the &ldquo;policy pivot.&rdquo; However, the path is uneven:</p>
        <div class="inflation-items">
          <div class="inflation-item">
            <div class="inflation-icon down">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="23 6 13.5 15.5 8.5 10.5 1 18"/><polyline points="17 6 23 6 23 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="inflation-text-title">Global Headline Inflation Declining</div>
              <div class="inflation-text-desc">Expected to continue falling through 2026 across most economies, enabling monetary easing.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="inflation-item">
            <div class="inflation-icon sticky">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="inflation-text-title">US Inflation Above Target Longer</div>
              <div class="inflation-text-desc">Projected to return to target more gradually than in other advanced economies, delaying rate cuts.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="inflation-item">
            <div class="inflation-icon up">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="23 18 13.5 8.5 8.5 13.5 1 6"/><polyline points="17 18 23 18 23 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="inflation-text-title">Sticky Services Inflation</div>
              <div class="inflation-text-desc">Services inflation has been particularly resistant, slowing the overall disinflation process globally.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="inflation-item">
            <div class="inflation-icon new">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="inflation-text-title">Renewed Pressures (Apr 2026)</div>
              <div class="inflation-text-desc">New inflationary pressures from defense spending and supply disruptions re-emerged by April 2026.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- POLICY EVOLUTION - LEFT COLUMN -->
      <section class="section section-left animate delay-4" aria-label="Evolving Policy Priorities">
        <div class="section-label">Section 04</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Evolving Policy Priorities</h2>
        <p class="section-body" style="margin-bottom:12px;">IMF policy guidance has shifted meaningfully from monetary stabilization to fiscal resilience to defense-spending management.</p>
        <div class="policy-timeline">
          <div class="policy-item">
            <div class="policy-period">Mid-2024</div>
            <div class="policy-focus">Manage disinflation; begin monetary easing carefully</div>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item">
            <div class="policy-period">Late 2024</div>
            <div class="policy-focus">Pivot monetary policy; ensure fiscal sustainability</div>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item shift">
            <div class="policy-period">Early 2025</div>
            <div class="policy-focus">Rebuild fiscal buffers; address demographic and gender gaps</div>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item shift">
            <div class="policy-period">Mid-2025</div>
            <div class="policy-focus">Restore confidence and predictability amid tariff uncertainty</div>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item shift">
            <div class="policy-period">Late 2025</div>
            <div class="policy-focus">Strengthen policy frameworks; cautious industrial policy</div>
          </div>
          <div class="policy-item shift">
            <div class="policy-period">Early 2026</div>
            <div class="policy-focus">Agile policy; manage defense-spending trade-offs; lay foundations for recovery</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- THEMES - RIGHT COLUMN -->
      <section class="section section-right animate delay-4" aria-label="Special Analytical Themes">
        <div class="section-label">Section 05</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Special Themes Across WEO Editions</h2>
        <p class="section-body" style="margin-bottom:16px;">Each WEO features deep-dive analytical chapters reflecting the IMF's broadening lens beyond macroeconomic stabilization.</p>
        <div class="themes-grid">
          <div class="theme-card">
            <div class="theme-card-number">01</div>
            <div class="theme-card-title">Monetary Policy in Global Disinflation</div>
            <div class="theme-card-desc">Examining the role of synchronized monetary tightening and its varied transmission across economies.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="theme-card">
            <div class="theme-card-number">02</div>
            <div class="theme-card-title">Social Acceptability of Reforms</div>
            <div class="theme-card-desc">Why some structural reforms face public resistance and how to design politically durable policy packages.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="theme-card">
            <div class="theme-card-number">03</div>
            <div class="theme-card-title">Industrial Policy: Effectiveness &amp; Cost</div>
            <div class="theme-card-desc">Assessing the fiscal cost and economic effectiveness of the new wave of industrial policies worldwide.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="theme-card">
            <div class="theme-card-number">04</div>
            <div class="theme-card-title">Inclusive Growth: Demographics &amp; Labor</div>
            <div class="theme-card-desc">Aging populations, gender disparities, and migrant skill alignment as drivers of long-term growth potential.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

    <!-- ===== FOOTER ===== -->
    <footer class="poster-footer">
      <div><span class="source-label">Sources:</span> IMF World Economic Outlook series, July 2024 &ndash; April 2026 (8 editions). Data reflects projections as of each publication date.</div>
      <div>IMF-World Bank Annual Meetings &bull; Research Symposium &bull; 2026</div>
    </footer>

  </main>

  <script>
    // === Menu ===
    function toggleMenu() {
      var dropdown = document.getElementById('vizMenuDropdown');
